; IDENTITY, as the card's is. A snap zone seats an object by composing its grab
; point, so this being the origin is what makes the slot's own transform the
; whole of the seating geometry. One seat serves both only because the origin
; is the same distance from the connector end on both -- see the note on the
; body above; the matching axes alone were not enough.
[node name="GrabPoint" type="Marker3D" parent="."]
visible = false
script = ExtResource("3_grabpoint")

